cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the preprint below. The Spanish version is under review at Texto Livre."
title: "Aligning Language Models with Indigenous Community Cosmovision through Constitutional AI"
abstract: >-
  This work presents a complete system for aligning language models with the
  ethical and philosophical principles of indigenous communities in Latin
  America. Based on interviews with five community leaders and defenders who
  are members of URI (United Religions Initiative), we built an operational
  cultural constitution grounded in an Indigenous community cosmovision, with
  12 principles covering territory, coexistence, authority, well-being,
  technology, and language. On this basis, we implemented the Constitutional
  AI (CAI) pipeline in two phases: supervised fine-tuning (SFT) with a
  self-critique and constitution-guided revision loop, and direct preference
  optimization (DPO) with 24 pairs of aligned and misaligned responses. The
  base models were Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct and Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct, both with
  LoRA adaptation. Three experimental configurations were run to estimate the
  robustness of results. The system was deployed in a conversational interface
  with retrieval-augmented generation (RAG).
